WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.600
Researcher Martin pushed the deck against
the door, hoping it would hold long enough

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.370
for him to find an alternate escape route.

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:10.950
He wasn’t thinking about the long term,
he couldn’t afford to.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.790
With the Foundation’s global reach, he’d
never truly escape them, never be able to

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:20.810
make it away, condemned to spend the rest
of his life on the run from the organization

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:22.689
he’d devoted his life to.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:27.900
It was too overwhelming to even attempt to
reckon with that, especially with the pounding

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.849
of a fist against the door.

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:34.559
He scrabbled around, opening windows to try
and see if there was a safe way down.

00:00:34.559 --> 00:00:39.170
Technically none of this was his fault, at
least in his mind.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:42.930
The administrative login information he’d
used to access the file shouldn’t have been

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:48.610
left so easy to find; that was just poor cyber
security on the Foundation’s part.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:54.880
Researcher Martin had been tasked with compiling
information on SCP-001, one of the most infamous

00:00:54.880 --> 00:01:00.250
anomalies ever encountered in the Foundation’s
long and storied history… or multiple of

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.660
them, at least.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.870
What Martin had come to learn was, there were
numerous entries within the Foundation’s

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:10.650
files that all acted as proposals for SCP-001.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:15.740
Some were creatures, the typical kind of anomalous
entities the Foundation dealt with on a regular

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:16.740
basis.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:22.720
But some of the proposals focused on more
abstract anomalies… and somehow, those were

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:28.670
more existentially terrifying than any evil
godlike being bent on destroying reality.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:33.729
Theories about the very source of anomalies
themselves, that their very existence might

00:01:33.729 --> 00:01:37.750
have been pre-determined by some otherworldly
force.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:43.979
Then there were the other proposals that named
parts of the Foundation as the true SCP-001.

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:49.060
Those seemed to suck Researcher Martin in
like a vortex, dragging him down a deep, dark

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:53.420
rabbit hole that made him start to question
everything he thought he knew about working

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.219
for the SCP Foundation.

00:01:55.219 --> 00:02:00.580
And the one that toppled him into a full-blown
conspiracy-obsessed stupor that there was

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:04.659
no coming back from: the Noir Box Proposal.

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:09.270
The weighted head of a battering ram splintered
the wooden surface of the door, spraying fragments

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.421
over the room.

00:02:10.421 --> 00:02:15.269
The table propped up to keep it shut toppled
under the force of entry, as a squad of shadowy

00:02:15.269 --> 00:02:18.700
figures in full black combat gear rushed inside.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.650
The Mobile Task Force surrounded the cowering
researcher, keeping their weapons trained

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:23.670
on him.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:26.920
Researcher Martin, pleading for his life,
started gesturing to the walls of the room

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:32.150
around him, that had been plastered with hastily
scrawled diagrams and equations.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:36.840
Martin tried desperately to find some concise,
easy-to-understand way of explaining to the

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.080
soldiers what he’d uncovered.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:44.090
They only picked up on a few words like ‘many
worlds hypothesis’ and ‘splitting universes’

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:48.820
but ultimately they didn’t follow what he
was saying – and weren’t sent there to

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:49.820
hear him out.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:54.590
All the MTF had been told was that Researcher
Martin had breached Foundation security and

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:58.629
now posed a risk of exposing sensitive information
about SCP-001.

00:02:58.629 --> 00:03:03.700
There was only one path of recourse: termination.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:08.000
However, unbeknownst to them, Doctor Martin
was fine.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.530
At least a version of him was, one who never
learned about the Noir Box Proposal for SCP-001,

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:17.620
and hadn’t gone mad trying to unravel its
mysteries.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:22.780
Instead, he was a respected higher ranking
member of the Foundation who was alive and

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:26.220
well… in a completely different timeline.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:31.209
The formation of the SCP Foundation has always
been shrouded in mystery, with nobody really

00:03:31.209 --> 00:03:36.680
knowing what the true origin of the organization
is and what is merely just a cover story left

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:39.849
in the archives to keep the truth hidden.

00:03:39.849 --> 00:03:45.690
SCP-001, the Noir Box Proposal at least, might
hold the answers to the questions surrounding

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:49.799
how the Foundation came to be – three times
over.

00:03:49.799 --> 00:03:54.989
Known as the Tindalos Trinity, the file pertaining
to this anomaly is buried deep in the SCP

00:03:54.989 --> 00:03:59.890
Foundation’s database, under layers upon
layers of encryption and security clearance

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:01.190
requirements.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:06.030
It requires someone at the very top level
of the Foundation to access, a member of either

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:10.189
the Overseer Council… or the Foundation’s
High Command… or Overwatch?

00:04:10.189 --> 00:04:12.209
But wait, what are those?

00:04:12.209 --> 00:04:14.620
Aren’t they all the same thing?

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:17.169
Well, yes and no.

00:04:17.169 --> 00:04:21.130
The exact name of the high-ranking secretive
group that runs the Foundation has often been

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:26.430
interchangeable, whether they’re known as
the O5 Council, the Overseer Council, et cetera.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:31.509
But what if that wasn’t just many different
names for the same governing body, but actually

00:04:31.509 --> 00:04:37.340
separate names for alternate versions of the
ones who control the SCP Foundation.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:38.910
Allow us to explain.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:44.190
All three of these groups - the Overseer Council,
High Command, and Overwatch – have come

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:49.070
to a consensus that SCP-001 is an anomaly
that connects to do with the Foundation’s

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:50.630
very origin.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:57.690
They believe that the founder of the SCP Foundation,
also known as SCP-001, was anomalous in some

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:02.820
way that caused them to interact with time
in an unusual way.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:07.490
The triumvirate of councils are in agreement
that around the time that the SCP Foundation

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:12.621
was formed, three distinct timelines were
generated, given the anomalous nature of the

00:05:12.621 --> 00:05:14.550
organization’s founder.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:20.220
Each one of these timelines drastically altered
the nature of SCP-001, featuring a different

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.430
version in each one.

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:26.990
In the first, commonly known as Timeline HC
– where the Foundation is run by a High

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:31.710
Command – SCP-001 was an anomalous human
corpse.

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:36.680
This timeline’s SCP-001 still exhibited
all the behavioral characteristics of a normal

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:41.980
human being, but could additionally replicate
itself at an erratic, uncontrollable rate

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:46.860
– usually when performing tasks that could
have multiple possible outcomes.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:53.460
SCP-001 in Timeline HC also interacted anachronistically
with its environment, passing through solid

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:56.669
matter that predated it or would outlast it.

00:05:56.669 --> 00:06:02.840
So, it had to be contained in a room that
was constructed before it existed as an anomaly.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:08.449
This timeline’s SCP-001 was responsible
for conceiving the idea for the SCP Foundation,

00:06:08.449 --> 00:06:12.530
and was able to promote a significant interest
in the organization.

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:17.060
However, they were assassinated before the
Foundation was officially codified, with the

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:22.010
culprits being a version of Mobile Task Force
Alp 0, who are believed to have originated

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:24.009
from either of the other two timelines.

00:06:24.009 --> 00:06:28.910
While this seems to have been done to deter
the Foundation forming in this timeline, it

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:31.360
seems to have had the opposite effect.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:37.860
Despite the assassination of SCP-001, occurring
before the official formation of the SCP Foundation

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:43.100
in Timeline HC, this version of the Foundation
was successfully codified by the thirteen

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:46.820
members of what they referred to as High Command.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:52.300
Given the anomalous circumstances around the
death of SCP-001, it provided a catalyst for

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:57.300
the organization to immediately establish
itself as this timeline’s protection against

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.660
the threat posed by anomalous entities.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:06.300
The body of SCP-001 was placed in the building
that had been its childhood home, securing

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:10.810
it somewhere that predated them to negate
their anomalous properties.

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:16.530
This made them the first anomaly contained
by Timeline HC’s version of the SCP Foundation,

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:20.610
posthumously garnering them the official designation
of SCP-001.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:24.670
So, that’s the first of our three timelines
at play.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:28.600
The events that unfold in the second are considerably
different.

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:35.479
In this timeline – Timeline OC – the Foundation
was initially created by a different SCP-001.

00:07:35.479 --> 00:07:40.600
This entity, referred to primarily as The
Founder (appropriately enough) was a human

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:44.360
being known to possess anomalous temporal
abilities.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:48.690
The Founder was known to also be immortal,
showing no visible signs of aging and with

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:53.330
a resistance to external damage that prevented
him from being directly killed.

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:57.979
Any injuries he sustained could be healed,
but only at the same rate typical of an average

00:07:57.979 --> 00:07:59.310
human being.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:03.509
The temporal side of his anomalous properties
pertained to predicting the future.

00:08:03.509 --> 00:08:08.810
The Founder was able to, with an inarguable
level of precision and accuracy, forecast

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:10.750
events before they occurred.

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:15.270
His foresight, it appeared to the Foundation,
was not inciting these events to happen as

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:21.420
he predicted them, however everything he ever
predicted would occur became an inevitability,

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:25.830
impossible to delay, avert or alter through
any means.

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:31.030
During the events of Timeline OC – and as
his preferred nickname implies – the Founder

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:36.060
was the sole figure responsible for establishing
this version of the SCP Foundation.

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:40.529
In this course of events, the O5 Council of
this timeline were known as the Overseer Council.

00:08:40.529 --> 00:08:45.450
It was, however, while he was in the process
of establishing the organization, that things

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:47.500
started to go awry.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:51.940
Whether he was able to predict this occurrence
or not is unknown, although it seems to have

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:59.029
corresponded with the MTF Alp 0 assassination
of SCP-001 in the other timeline, Timeline

00:08:59.029 --> 00:09:00.029
HC.

00:09:00.029 --> 00:09:05.570
In Timeline OC, at the same time as the assassination
in Timeline HC, all the Founder began to exhibit

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:10.080
his anomalous temporal properties in front
of the original members of Overseer Council.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:15.640
However, it should also be noted that there
was no recorded presence of MTF Alp 0 in Timeline

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:16.640
OC.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:22.010
Believing the Founder to be a potential danger
to the Foundation they had all helped to create,

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:25.510
the founding Overseer Council classified him
as an anomalous threat.

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:30.079
They immediately devised a set of containment
measures for the Founder – now designating

00:09:30.079 --> 00:09:37.080
him as SCP-001, the first anomaly contained
by this timeline’s version of the Foundation.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:42.220
He was placed within a standard humanoid containment
cell, and given regular meals, while personnel

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:44.800
were forbidden to communicate with him.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:50.040
Given his role in establishing the Foundation
in this version of events, SCP-001 is, naturally,

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:54.280
in favor of containing and analyzing anomalies.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:59.040
However, not when that includes him, and insisted
that he be released.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:03.510
According to one of his predictions for forthcoming
events, he requested to be allowed to build

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:08.160
a device, but refused to elaborate on the
intended purpose of it.

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:13.050
SCP-001 even refused to allow other members
of Foundation personnel to construct the device

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:15.930
on his behalf for testing purposes.

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:20.820
The third of these timelines is referred to
as Timeline OW, wherein the leading body of

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:23.010
the Foundation are known as Overwatch.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:28.370
Here, just like the previous iterations of
its history, the description of SCP-001 and

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:31.520
their role in forming the SCP Foundation differs.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:37.550
In this timeline, SCP-001 is an anomaly that
consists of two distinct parts.

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:41.430
The first of these is a figure not dissimilar
from the Founder.

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:47.610
Referred to as SCP-001-1, this person is also
a functionally immortal human, who doesn’t

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:50.880
age and can’t heal rapidly from damage.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:57.360
SCP-001-1 also advocates for securing and
analyzing anomalies, however, this includes

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:00.500
himself, as he doesn’t object to his own
containment.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:04.940
Or that of the second component of this SCP-001.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:11.350
Known as SCP-001-A, this device is capable
of accurately calculating any and all possible

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:14.660
outcomes of any event that is input into it.

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:19.300
Unlike the Founder, who seemed to possess
a foresight able to predict the only inevitable

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:25.980
outcome of the future, SCP-001-A is able to
account for the possibility of multiple potential

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:30.790
futures, even down to accounting for how its
own predictions could potentially influence

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.490
or alter outcomes.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:39.940
In laymen’s terms, at least one of the eventualities
predicted by SCP-001-A will always be accurate.

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:46.070
Unless the predictions are to do with its
own future, or the future of SCP-001-1.

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:50.050
In this instance, the device will always produce
one of two assumptions that are incorrect.

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:55.500
Either that SCP-001-1 was killed after an
assassination attempt and never constructed

00:11:55.500 --> 00:12:03.310
SCP-001-A. But that’s impossible, after
all, SCP-001-A exists, it’s already been

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:05.060
made in this timeline.

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:11.060
The other incorrect prediction it can give
is that SCP-001-1 also exhibits the same anomalous

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:17.470
properties as the prediction machine – more
akin to the Founder – and that SCP-001-A

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:19.730
was never constructed in the first place.

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:24.100
But again, that can’t be right… in this
timeline, anyway.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:31.060
According to records, within Timeline OW,
their version of the Founder – who is, of

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:34.750
course, SCP-001-1 – encountered a version
of Mobile Task Force Alp 0 from one of the

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:36.250
other timelines.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:40.730
They presented the Founder of the OW timeline
with detailed blueprints for the construction

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:43.260
of SCP-001-A.

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:48.790
The device’s completion coincided with the
assassination in Timeline HC and the corresponding

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:52.010
anomalous incident in Timeline OC.

00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:56.300
After this point, MTF Alp 0 departs from Timeline
OW.

00:12:56.300 --> 00:13:03.190
This version of the SCP Foundation is then
created to study the device, SCP-001-A, with

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:08.920
this Founder and a group of his close friends,
who would become this Foundation’s Overwatch.

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:12.709
Following this initial research group’s
discovery of other anomalous phenomena that

00:13:12.709 --> 00:13:17.639
threatened the rest of society, the team’s
goal expanded to research anomalies and protect

00:13:17.639 --> 00:13:19.930
the world from the danger they posed.

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:24.670
However, the rest of the Overwatch began to
age at a natural rate, while the Founder didn’t

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:29.770
recognize this, he volunteered to be contained
and studied, thus becoming a component of

00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:33.060
this timeline’s SCP-001.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:37.089
Stepping back and looking at all of these
timelines, there seems to be a number of marked

00:13:37.089 --> 00:13:42.389
similarities, particularly relating to how
the Foundation was established and how a figure

00:13:42.389 --> 00:13:47.040
– usually the one who founded the organization
– possessed anomalous means of interacting

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:49.170
with time and temporality.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:54.240
Under normal circumstances, interaction between
alternate timelines should be impossible.

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:58.680
But the preservation of information about
all three on the SCP Foundation’s database

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:03.110
has somehow enabled all three timelines to
communicate with each other.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:07.860
Through exchanging intelligence via their
own versions of the database, all three iterations

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:12.720
of the Foundation across the three timelines
have learned that almost all of the anomalies

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:17.630
they have encountered since being established
are exclusive to their own timeline.

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:22.940
There are a total of seventeen anomalies that
have been confirmed to exist across the three

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:23.940
timelines.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:26.190
But there’s a concerning factor in all of
this.

00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:31.550
The presence of an anachronistic military
group referring to itself as MTF Alp 0.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:36.430
This Mobile Task Force’s direct involvement
in the events of both Timeline HC – where

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:42.200
they assassinated SCP-001 – and Timeline
OW – where they provided schematics for

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:46.440
SCP-001-A – raises an awful lot of questions.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:52.150
This MTF had to have been acting on orders
of the Foundation, but which version in which

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:53.250
timeline?

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:58.389
The consensus among the leading committees
of all three, the High Command, Overseer Council,

00:14:58.389 --> 00:15:03.220
and Overwatch, is that at some unknown date
in the future, each of them will inevitably

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:09.410
send their own version of MTF Alp 0 back in
time to alter the Foundation’s past.

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:13.960
And in a sense, they’ve already done it
and seen how this altered the circumstances

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:16.990
in order to inadvertently create the Foundation.

00:15:16.990 --> 00:15:23.050
But this poses the risk of one of these timelines
overwriting another, thus meaning all information

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:26.769
gathered by alternate iterations of the Foundation
could be lost.

00:15:26.769 --> 00:15:31.720
So, putting their heads together, these Foundation
leading committees come to the conclusion

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:35.180
that they need to attempt to merge all three
timelines.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:40.250
And it seems the way to do so is using the
device that Timeline OC’s Founder wanted

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:44.740
to build, and that Timeline OW’s Founder
was able to construct.

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:51.620
This device is how this proposal for SCP-001
was given its nickname; the Noir Box.

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:57.120
The intention of the Noir Box is to shunt
all three timelines into a stable, joint path,

00:15:57.120 --> 00:16:00.339
like turning loose strands into a single length
of twine.

00:16:00.339 --> 00:16:04.940
As such, the leading committees of all three
different timelines have agreed to share their

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:10.810
intel on how each of them can safely create
their own Noir Boxes, and all three will be

00:16:10.810 --> 00:16:13.720
used to merge the timelines.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:18.380
Every member of High Command, the Overseer
Council, and Overwatch sign off on it.

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:21.810
But whether or not the plan works is another
matter.

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:28.490
The fabric of time is delicate, and one wrong
move could tear everything apart…

00:16:28.490 --> 00:16:33.890
Now check out “SCP-001 NOIR BOX PROPOSAL
- HATED CAESAR” and “SCP-001 OVERLORD

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:35.090
CENSURE” for more!

